Guidelines for drinking-water quality — WHO, 2026 consolidated edition (@wu-who: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_71BB45J2CZ76C0WZ6H1C7SWZ5F
World Health Organization. Guidelines for drinking-water quality, fourth edition incorporating the first, second and third addenda, 17 June 2026. ISBN 9789240121225. [Official edition, complete download and individual chapters](https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240121225).

Read chapters 1–5 for the public-health framework, targets, water safety planning and surveillance. Continue through the circumstances, microbial, chemical, radiological and acceptability chapters, then use the relevant fact sheets and analytical/treatment annexes for a particular question. This is international guidance that informs national standards; jurisdictional requirements need their own sources.

The official page identifies 647 pages and the 2026 third-addendum changes. Its chapter index was inspected; automated retrieval of the complete IRIS-hosted PDF returned 403, so full page-by-page inspection is not claimed. Use the official chapter links if the whole-file host is unavailable. Preserve the edition's actual rights and third-party notices. The older 2022 two-addendum edition is a distinct version.

